# ADAPT environment template
#
# Quick setup from the repository root:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   cd frontend && npm ci
#   npm run dev
#
# The backend reads this file from the repository root no matter whether it is
# started from Adapt/ or Adapt/backend/. Defaults are safe, so every setting
# below is optional unless you are changing that behavior.

# ---- backend -------------------------------------------------------------
ADAPT_MODE=local
# Trusted LAN demo only: consent-only guests, three short games, local engine.
# Single API worker; do not enable on a public deployment. See docs/CAPACITY.md.
ADAPT_DEMO_MODE=false
ADAPT_FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
ADAPT_DB_ENCRYPTION=auto
ADAPT_VOICE_ENABLED=true
ADAPT_ALLOW_LOCAL_FALLBACK=true
ADAPT_RATE_LIMIT_MULTIPLIER=1
# Trust forwarding headers only when the direct peer is your reverse proxy.
# Comma-separated IP addresses; empty means direct Internet clients cannot spoof their bucket.
# ADAPT_TRUSTED_PROXIES=127.0.0.1,::1

# Keep learner data in the default repo-local var/ directory. If you move it,
# use an absolute path; relative paths are resolved from the process directory.
# ADAPT_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/adapt-data
# ADAPT_DB_PATH=/absolute/path/to/adapt-data/adapt.db

# Encryption: the default generates var/keys/adapt.key on first start. Back it
# up with the database. Alternatively use ONE of these, never both:
# ADAPT_KEYFILE=/absolute/path/to/adapt.key
# ADAPT_DB_KEY=base64-encoded-32-byte-key
# ADAPT_DB_PASSPHRASE=use-a-long-private-passphrase

# ---- Three dedicated AI API slots (console-only, never sent to the browser) ----
# Manage keys interactively via `adapt config set-key --service <name>` and custom
# HTTPS endpoints via `adapt config set-url --slot <ai1|ai2|ai3>`.
#
# Slot 1 — AI 1 (Psychology & Learning-Science API):
# Pulls empirical cognitive-science / educational-psychology findings into learner
# hypotheses and proposals (OpenAlex, NCBI PubMed, Psychologie et Serenite, or a
# custom HTTPS psychology site API).
# ADAPT_AI1_PSYCHOLOGY_ENABLED=false
# ADAPT_AI1_API_URL=
# ADAPT_AI1_API_KEY=
# ADAPT_AI1_API_HEADER=Authorization
# ADAPT_PUBMED_API_KEY=
# ADAPT_GEMINI_MODEL_AI1=
#
# Slot 2 — AI 2 (Education Content API):
# Pulls verified curriculum explanations, key facts, definitions, and misconceptions
# into ContentPacks and live tutoring (Oak National Academy Open API, Wikipedia /
# Wikibooks plain-text extracts, or a custom HTTPS education site API).
# ADAPT_AI2_EDUCATION_ENABLED=false
# ADAPT_AI2_API_URL=
# ADAPT_AI2_API_KEY=
# ADAPT_AI2_API_HEADER=Authorization
# ADAPT_OAK_API_KEY=
# ADAPT_GEMINI_MODEL_AI2=
#
# Slot 3 — AI 3 (Lesson Adaptation API):
# Adapts AI 1's learner state + AI 2's educational pack into step-sized, whole-plan
# validated lessons (custom HTTPS adaptation endpoint, OpenAI-compatible
# /chat/completions endpoint, or a dedicated Gemini key/model).
# ADAPT_AI3_API_URL=
# ADAPT_AI3_API_KEY=
# ADAPT_AI3_API_HEADER=Authorization
# ADAPT_GEMINI_MODEL_AI3=
#
# ---- shared / optional services ------------------------------------------
# Leave the Gemini line commented for the deterministic local tutor. If you
# configure it, restart the app after saving the key. Never commit a real key.
# ADAPT_GEMINI_API_KEY=paste-your-gemini-key-here
# ADAPT_YOUTUBE_API_KEY=paste-your-youtube-key-here
# ADAPT_GEMINI_DAILY_CALL_BUDGET=120
# ADAPT_GEMINI_DAILY_TOKEN_BUDGET=2000000
#
# Which model answers each class of work. The defaults are the provider's rolling
# aliases, because versioned IDs get retired without notice (a key created in
# October 2026 got "404 ... no longer available to new users" for gemini-2.5-flash
# while that ID was still on the same key's model list). An alias tracks whatever
# the provider serves now; pin a versioned ID when a result has to be reproducible,
# and expect to move the pin yourself.
# ADAPT_GEMINI_MODEL_LIGHT=gemini-flash-lite-latest
# ADAPT_GEMINI_MODEL_STANDARD=gemini-flash-latest
# ADAPT_GEMINI_MODEL_DEEP=gemini-pro-latest
# Optional: try this model first when a configured model ID returns 404. If it is
# unset (or is also gone) the client tries another class, then discovers a
# replacement from this key's own model list and remembers it for the process.
# ADAPT_GEMINI_MODEL_FALLBACK=
# Safety threshold sent with every request (provider's own value names).
# ADAPT_GEMINI_SAFETY_THRESHOLD=BLOCK_MEDIUM_AND_ABOVE

# Optional browser/API settings for `cd frontend && npm run dev:web` or
# `npm run start`. `npm run dev` / `npm run host` set ADAPT_API themselves.
# The frontend loader reads only these allowlisted names from this root file;
# provider credentials are never copied into the Node or browser environment.
# ADAPT_API=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PORT=3000
# ADAPT_DEV_ORIGIN=localhost,127.0.0.1
